    "For \\(< 0\\) the answer is BETWEEN the roots; for \\(> 0\\) it is OUTSIDE them. Use \\(\\le\\) or \\(\\ge\\) only when the line sits under the sign."
   ],
   "title": "Bronze: reading a squared inequality",
   "example": {
